{
  "totalDuration": 39.995,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "text": "If you spent four hundred dollars on a flight today, the airline lost money on you.",
      "start": 0.15,
      "speechEnd": 4.865,
      "end": 5.145,
      "duration": 4.995
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Jet fuel, pilot wages, and airport gate fees vaporize almost every cent, leaving just twelve dollars in profit.",
      "start": 5.145,
      "speechEnd": 13.251,
      "end": 13.531,
      "duration": 8.387
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Yet major airlines still report billions in annual profit. If flying planes destroys cash, where does the money come from?",
      "start": 13.531,
      "speechEnd": 21.745,
      "end": 22.025,
      "duration": 8.493
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "Buried inside Delta's S E C filing is the truth: American Express paid them six point five billion dollars just for frequent flyer miles.",
      "start": 22.025,
      "speechEnd": 32.115,
      "end": 32.395,
      "duration": 10.371
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Airlines aren't airlines anymore. They are unregulated banks with wings, and the planes are just the bait.",
      "start": 32.395,
      "speechEnd": 39.265,
      "end": 39.545,
      "duration": 7.149
    }
  ],
